# BuildKit uses this file INSTEAD OF .dockerignore when building with
# `-f Dockerfile-ptools` (it does not merge with it), so this is a standalone
# allowlist rather than a copy of the root ignore file.
#
# Dockerfile-ptools consumes exactly two paths from the context -- the aic-export
# archive it ADDs, and the vendor overlay it COPYs on top -- so ignore everything
# and opt those back in. Keep the archive filename in sync with the ADD line when
# upgrading Pathway Tools; the older archives in assets/ptools/ stay excluded.
#
# NOTE: every COPY/ADD source in Dockerfile-ptools must be opted in here or the
# build fails with "failed to calculate checksum ... not found". No CI job builds
# this image (CI builds sms-api only; ptools is hand-built via
# kustomize/scripts/build_and_push.sh), so an omission here is invisible until
# someone builds by hand.
*
!assets/ptools/aic-export-30.0.tar.gz
!assets/ptools/overrides/htdocs/sms/sms.js
